{"name":"Baby Girl","hex":"#ffdfe8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby girl","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female baby.","Friendly or intimate term of address for a woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby_girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baby Girl (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Baby Girl is the first album released by May J. under the label Sony Music Japan.\nThe album charted on the weekly Oricon chart on the #50 place."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Baby_Girl_%28album%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Girl_(album)"},{"title":"Baby Girl (Sugarland song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Baby Girl\" is a song co-written and recorded by American country music group Sugarland. Originally released in 2003 as part of Premium Quality Tunes, it was re-released in July 2004 as the first single from the group's debut album Twice the Speed of Life."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/BabyGirl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Girl_(Sugarland_song)"},{"title":"Baby Girl (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Baby Girl is a 2026 Indian Malayalam-language medical thriller film directed by Arun Varma and written by the screenwriter duo Bobby–Sanjay. The film is produced by Listin Stephen under the banner of Magic Frames. It stars Nivin Pauly, Sangeeth Prathap, Lijomol Jose, Abhimanyu Shammi Thilakan, Aditi Ravi, Azees Nedumangad, and Aswanth Lal."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Baby_Girl_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Girl_(film)"},{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AViews_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/500px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/1280px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/500px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eight-month-old infant; as a common feature, eyes are usually large in relation to the face.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaby_Face.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg/500px-Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg/500px-Baby_h